From: retro98boy <retro98boy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: rockchip: keep the RK3562 VIO interconnect clock enabled

ACLK_TOP_VIO supplies the shared video interconnect. The RK3562 TRM,
section 2.10.6, requires this clock for the VO, VI and VDPU buses.
The clock tree does not represent these bus dependencies.

Disabling this clock causes VI idle requests to time out. Subsequent
power-domain shutdown attempts fault while saving ISP QoS registers.
The fault leaves power-domain locks held, blocking device probing and
shutdown on KICKPI K3B.

Keep this shared interconnect clock critical, like ACLK_TOP.
Leave individual device clocks and power-domain gating unchanged.
---
 drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c
--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3562.c
@@ -236,7 +236,7 @@ static struct rockchip_clk_branch rk3562_clk_branches[] __initdata = {
-	COMPOSITE(ACLK_TOP_VIO, "aclk_top_vio", gpll_cpll_p, 0,
+	COMPOSITE(ACLK_TOP_VIO, "aclk_top_vio", gpll_cpll_p, CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 			RK3562_CLKSEL_CON(5), 15, 1, MFLAGS, 8, 4, DFLAGS,
 			RK3562_CLKGATE_CON(1), 1, GFLAGS),
 	COMPOSITE(CLK_24M_SSCSRC, "clk_24m_sscsrc", vpll_dmyhpll_gpll_cpll_p, 0,
 			RK3562_CLKSEL_CON(6), 6, 2, MFLAGS, 0, 6, DFLAGS,
 			RK3562_CLKGATE_CON(1), 9, GFLAGS),
 	COMPOSITE(CLK_CAM0_OUT2IO, "clk_cam0_out2io", gpll_cpll_xin24m_dmyapll_p, 0,
